From e0db373281bd5b97fe6b483309567d70da0f7069 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HampterDev <131729366+HampterDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:40:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Stop reading face charsets past the 12-entry table

text_dc_select_font took the charset of face 0 for faces 0x14 and up
with language index 0, and g_3dDevice.faceCharsets[face] otherwise. The
table has 12 entries and faces go up to 0x1d (SCDream), so faces 12-0x13
with any language index, and faces 0x14-0x1d with every other language
index, read the bytes after it, in hexDigitFlags.

Faces past the table now get, without the read, the charset that those
bytes gave them where it mattered:

- Faces 12-0x13 read 0 and get ANSI_CHARSET (0).
- SCDream read 0x10101, which CreateFontA and the LOGFONT of the font
  file truncate to DEFAULT_CHARSET, and gets DEFAULT_CHARSET.
- The EOT faces 0x14-0x1c read 0, 0x101, 0x1010100 or 0x1010101 and get
  ANSI_CHARSET. eot_logfont puts a fixed charset 1 in their LOGFONT, and
  get_code_page_from_charset gives code page 1252 for all of these
  values, so only the font and extent cache keys change.

The purist branch made the same change in 103a473.

Validation: the new test_face_charset runs the extracted
text_dc_select_font with the production g_3dDevice initializer for faces
0-0x1d, language indexes 0-12, five service types and two folder
languages: faces in the table, and faces 0x14 and up with language index
0, keep the old value; the others get the values above, with the bytes
the old lookup read checked against them and against their code page.
3900 selections; the test fails on the previous code. Release build
without warnings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaQB81YtRGLtH8zvfX7WTY
---
 src/render/textdc.c           | 12 ++++-
 tests/build.bat               |  3 ++
 tests/build_face_charset.bat  | 15 ++++++
 tests/extract_face_charset.py | 28 +++++++++++
 tests/test_face_charset.c     | 93 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 150 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/build_face_charset.bat
 create mode 100644 tests/extract_face_charset.py
 create mode 100644 tests/test_face_charset.c

diff --git a/src/render/textdc.c b/src/render/textdc.c
index f3affc0..eaa252c 100644
--- a/src/render/textdc.c
+++ b/src/render/textdc.c
@@ -111,7 +111,17 @@ void text_dc_select_font(struct TextDC *self, int a, int b, int c, int d)
     }
     self->face = face;
     self->size = size;
-    self->charset = (lang == 0 && face >= 0x14) ? g_3dDevice.faceCharsets[0] : g_3dDevice.faceCharsets[face];
+    /* faceCharsets has 12 entries; faces past it used to read the bytes after it, in
+       hexDigitFlags. Keep the values that mattered: SCDream read 0x10101, which fonts
+       truncate to DEFAULT_CHARSET, and faces 12-0x13 read ANSI_CHARSET. The EOT faces read
+       0, 0x101, 0x1010100 or 0x1010101, but their LOGFONT has a fixed charset, and like
+       ANSI_CHARSET each of these decodes text as code page 1252. */
+    if (lang == 0 && face >= FONT_FACE_EOT_FIRST)
+        self->charset = g_3dDevice.faceCharsets[0];
+    else if (face >= 0 && (size_t)face < sizeof g_3dDevice.faceCharsets / sizeof g_3dDevice.faceCharsets[0])
+        self->charset = g_3dDevice.faceCharsets[face];
+    else
+        self->charset = face == FONT_FACE_SCDREAM ? DEFAULT_CHARSET : ANSI_CHARSET;
     self->bold = (BYTE)c;
     self->italic = (BYTE)d;
 }
